From d4992738cb12aa91bdf20da6527b6cdc0f99455b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Clunis <andrew@orospakr.ca>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:37:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Input: synaptics - re-enable InterTouch on the ThinkPad
 T14/P14s Gen 1 AMD

Commit e4ce4d3a939d ("Input: synaptics - enable InterTouch on ThinkPad
T14/P14s Gen 1 AMD") added LEN2064 to smbus_pnp_ids, and commit
2fd003ee8ade ("Input: synaptics - disable Intertouch for Lenovo T14 and
P14s AMD G1") removed it again because SMBus Host Notify was not
available on these laptops.

The AMD FCH SMBus controller can provide Host Notify through its ASF
target block, which i2c-piix4 gains in a separate series. With that in
place, the Synaptics TM3471 in a T14 Gen 1 AMD (20UD, Ryzen 7 PRO 4750U,
BIOS 1.56) attaches as rmi4_smbus with 15 ms reports, keeps the
TrackPoint on the F03 pass-through, and survives suspend/resume.

Restore the entry. Where the adapter does not offer Host Notify,
psmouse_smbus_init() still refuses the SMBus companion and the pad stays
on PS/2, so the entry is inert there.
---
 drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c b/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c
index d920aee..fe16ff9 100644
--- a/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c
+++ b/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c
@@ -194,2 +194,3 @@ static const char * const smbus_pnp_ids[] = {
 	"LEN2068", /* T14 Gen 1 */
+	"LEN2064", /* T14 Gen 1 AMD / P14s Gen 1 AMD */
 	"LEN2073", /* T14/P14s Gen 2 AMD */
-- 
2.55.0

